    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d62">

                <pb facs="0121" n="109" xml:id="pg109"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">868.00/2–1245: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Greece</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">MacVeagh</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Athens</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1945-02-12">February 12,
                        1945</date>.<lb/>[Received February 12—10:45 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>166. See my 150 of February 7.<anchor n="39" xml:id="d62-f1"/> A Government
                    communiqué published in this morning’s papers announces that after a session
                    which lasted all night agreement was reached between the Government and EAM at
                    4:30 this morning. Messrs. Macmillan and Deeper were present. The members of the
                    respective deputations and the Secretary of the Conference signed a protocol in
                    which they “declare that they have reached complete agreement on all the matters
                    discussed during the Conference, and that a detailed text of the agreement is to
                    be signed today at 1400 hours”.<anchor n="40" xml:id="d62-f2"/>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">MacVeagh</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
